    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1202">

                <pb facs="0983" n="867" xml:id="pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/5433.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Vera Cruz to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-11-07T21:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1912—9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Profuse expressions of friendship for the United States are being made by
                    citizens and residents of the State and city of Vera Cruz; Commander Hughes is
                    virtually their hero now, and he is entitled to all the praise and credit given
                    him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
